course: dictionary
lesson: 9203
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word soil can mean three different things. Read the words around it to find out which one fits. «Mangroves ... their tangled roots break the waves and hold the soil» means the ground where plants grow.
explain: Soil can also mean land or a country, as in «on British soil». The clue is that the word talks about a whole land, not a patch of garden. Soil is also a verb: to soil something is to make it dirty. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If you swap in "ground" and the sentence still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Soil is the top layer of the ground, where plants grow.
fact: Soil is made of tiny bits of rock, dead plants and animals, water and air.
fact: Worms and tiny living things help make soil rich, and plant roots take water and minerals from it.
fact: Kinds of soil include sandy soil, clay soil and loamy soil.
fact: Soil can have germs, so wash your hands after gardening.
exercise: In «their tangled roots break the waves and hold the soil», what does soil mean? | A kind of wave | Water in a pond | Gold coins buried in the sand | *The ground where plants grow
exercise: «Muddy boots will soil the carpet.» What does soil mean here? | To dig a deep hole | *To make something dirty | To wash something clean | To grow plants
exercise: «The ginkgos sprouted again from their roots, kept safe under the soil.» Where were the roots kept safe? | *In the ground | Up in the clouds | In a glass jar on a shelf | In the sea
test: Soil is made of tiny bits of rock, dead plants and animals, water and air. Which of these is NOT in soil? | Tiny bits of rock | Dead plants and animals | Water and air | *Plastic bottles from the shop
test: Why should you wash your hands after gardening? | Because gardening is always messy and fun | Because soil is hot and dry | Because roots need soap | *Because soil can have germs
exam: «Farmers cut steps called terraces into the slopes, so the flat steps stop soil washing away.» What does soil mean in this sentence? | A country | *The top layer of ground | A kind of rock | To make dirty
